00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:53.190
inevitably comes disaster as it has through&nbsp;
all the ages of history so today blood fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:53.190 --> 00:21:58.290
and famine relentlessly persecute the human&nbsp;
race in this land of ours so bountifully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:02.730
supplied by nature with fertile lands and&nbsp;
rich forests disaster has taken a terrible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:07.350
toll raging floods have swept the green&nbsp;
valleys imprisoning great cities in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:11.340
grasp of icy waters leaving destruction&nbsp;
and the threat of disease in their wake

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:39.580
but in the moment of greatest need the&nbsp;
shaft troops of disaster go into action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:43.210
with the courage and perseverance which&nbsp;
armed our forefathers against despair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:48.340
the shock troops of disaster the great army&nbsp;
of WPA workers diverted from their work of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:53.050
construction and improvement to meet a pressing&nbsp;
emergency have proven their merit through many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:58.420
tragic hours which have carried a far-flung&nbsp;
areas of the nation working hand-in-hand with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:03.670
other agencies of relief the men and women of&nbsp;
the WPA take up the work of rescue evacuation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.670 --> 00:23:07.840
and relief but the first thought for the&nbsp;
saving of imperiled lives and the protection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:12.430
of threatened areas from advancing waters&nbsp;
the orderly program goes swiftly forward

00:23:25.110 --> 00:23:29.700
food is distributed to flood victims&nbsp;
from outdoor kitchens and car loads of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:34.680
warm clothes and bedding are rushed - shivering&nbsp;
refugees from WPA sewing rooms in many states

00:23:40.110 --> 00:23:45.120
in emergency hospitals thousands&nbsp;
of lives are saved by Red Cross&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:48.990
and volunteer nurses and doctors&nbsp;
assisted by trained WPA workers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:56.930 --> 00:24:01.850
for hundreds of miles along the flood&nbsp;
area the WPA supplies the shock troops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:01.850 --> 00:24:06.770
that hold the river within man-made walls&nbsp;
levee workers transport material by hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:06.770 --> 00:24:12.230
by truck by boat working day and night&nbsp;
they fill countless thousands of sandbags&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:12.230 --> 00:24:16.490
raising the levees above the record press&nbsp;
often working under the skilled direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:16.490 --> 00:24:19.400
of Army engineers relief workers&nbsp;
fight the flood at every point

00:24:34.280 --> 00:24:38.510
the people of the flood area will not&nbsp;
soon forget the courage of these heroic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:38.510 --> 00:24:41.900
workers for administrator Harry&nbsp;
Hopkins heard their praise along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:45.410
the full route of his inspection trip&nbsp;
as head of the President's Committee

